[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:The Dead Return]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:11.01]What happens to the lanterns at the end of the festival? | 节日结束时灯笼会怎么样？
[00:17.38]A Festival for the Dead is held once a year in Japan. | 日本每年举办一次“亡灵节”。
[00:22.72]This festival is a cheerful occasion, | 这个节日是个欢乐的日子，
[00:26.05]for on this day, the dead are said to return to their homes and they are welcomed by the living. | 因为据说这一天死去的人要回到自己的家里来，活着的人则对他们表示欢迎。
[00:34.36]As they are expected to be hungry after their long journey, food is laid out for them. | 因为预料他们在长途跋涉之后会饿，所以人们摆放好了饭菜。
[00:41.81]Specially-made lanterns are hung outside each house to help the dead to find their way. | 每家门前挂着特制的灯笼，帮助亡灵找到回家的路。
[00:49.85]All night long, people dance and sing. | 彻夜载歌载舞。
[00:54.07]In the early morning the food that had been laid out for the dead | 大清早，人们为亡灵摆放的饭菜
[00:59.49]is thrown into a river or into the sea as it is considered unlucky for anyone living to eat it. | 被扔进河里或海里，因为人们认为活人吃了这些饭菜是不吉利的。
[01:09.25]In towns that are near the sea, the tiny lanterns which had been hung in the streets the night before, | 在临海的城镇，头天夜里挂在大街上的小灯笼
[01:17.84]are placed into the water when the festival is over. | 在节后就放到水里去了。
[01:22.15]Thousands of lanterns slowly drift out to sea guiding the dead on their return journey to the other world. | 成千上万只灯笼慢慢漂向大海，为亡灵返回另一个世界引路。
[01:31.58]This is a moving spectacle, for crowds of people | 这是一个感人的场面，人们成群地
[01:36.07]stand on the shore watching the lanterns drifting away until they can be seen no more. | 站在岸边，注视着灯笼漂去，直到再也看不见为止。
